  "narrative": "All estimates below are already signed to each registered hypothesis direction, so positive signed estimates support the registered direction, negative signed estimates support the opposite direction, and intervals including zero leave the direction uncertain. The new direct subgroup analyses strongly corroborate the main accepted associations and reduce concern about batch- or subtype-driven artifacts. MSI-high cells showed much stronger WRN dependency in adenocarcinoma (signed mean_difference +0.784, 95% CI +0.748 to +0.820, R27) and in batch_a (+0.824, 95% CI +0.766 to +0.882, R28). These are close to the accepted main effect (+0.790) and are extremely large on the dependency scale, far exceeding any plausible 10%-relative benchmark and far larger than the confidence intervals expected for small false-positive effects. Therefore H39 and H45 are accepted and kept active as stability evidence for H8. SMARCA4-loss cells similarly showed much stronger SMARCA2 dependency in batch_a (+0.747, 95% CI +0.709 to +0.785, R29) and in adenocarcinoma (+0.777, 95% CI +0.755 to +0.799, R32), supporting H9 and making the earlier small batch interaction less concerning. TP53-intact cells showed stronger USP7 dependency in batch_a (+0.417, 95% CI +0.284 to +0.550, R30) and adenocarcinoma (+0.385, 95% CI +0.299 to +0.471, R34), supporting H12. KEAP1-loss cells showed the accepted less-negative/weaker NFE2L2 dependency in batch_a (+0.812, 95% CI +0.765 to +0.858, R31) and adenocarcinoma (+0.793, 95% CI +0.769 to +0.817, R33), supporting the reversed accepted association H13. These internal stratum estimates are not independent validation, but they indicate that the accepted effects remain large and directionally stable across major strata tested here. The marker-negative control H54 tested constructed marker D against SMARCA2 and found a tiny estimate (+0.002, 95% CI -0.030 to +0.035, R35). Given the very large accepted SMARCA4-SMARCA2 effect, this marker control is best interpreted as no marker-driven artifact on SMARCA2, so H54 is rejected and closed. The refinement testing whether TP53-intact cells have stronger MDM2 dependency when CDKN2A is intact was also null (+0.007, 95% CI -0.016 to +0.030, R38), consistent with the prior overall null for TP53 loss versus MDM2 dependency; H60 is rejected and closed. The MSI-high versus DHX9 test gave a small positive signed estimate (+0.017, 95% CI -0.017 to +0.052, R36), and the EGFR-amplification versus EGFR-dependency test restricted to KRAS- and PIK3CA-wild-type eligibility gave a small positive signed estimate (+0.020, 95% CI -0.011 to +0.052, R37). Both intervals include zero and point estimates are tiny relative to the accepted large associations, but their upper bounds are not small enough to exclude all effects that might be near the clinical significance threshold; H55 is deferred as a weak unresolved replication-stress candidate, and H59 is kept active because it belongs to an overall still-unresolved EGFR-dependency line of inquiry. The most important next validation is independent confirmation of the central MSI-high/WRN association H8. It is large, accepted, biologically interpretable, and currently supported by discovery data plus adenocarcinoma and batch_a internal stratum estimates, but it has not yet received independent validation.",
  "research_notes": "Updated accepted/stable evidence: H8 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency remains the leading unvalidated accepted association; H39 and H45 directly confirm within adenocarcinoma and batch_a, respectively. H9 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency remains accepted and validated, with direct batch_a and adenocarcinoma confirmations H46 and H49. H12 TP53 intact -> stronger USP7 dependency remains accepted but unvalidated; direct batch_a and adenocarcinoma confirmations H47 and H51 support stability. H13 KEAP1 loss -> less-negative/less dependent NFE2L2 remains accepted and validated, with direct batch_a and adenocarcinoma confirmations H48 and H50. Negative controls continue to argue against constructed-marker artifacts: H54 marker D versus SMARCA2 is null and closed. Weak unresolved leads: H55 MSI-high versus DHX9 is deferred; H59 EGFR amplification in KRAS/PIK3CA-wild-type eligibility is small positive and active, with H5 and H14 also still unresolved. Rejected/refined null: H60 TP53-intact MDM2 dependency in CDKN2A-intact cells is null/closed, consistent with H11. Validation request: H8 is prioritized because it is a central, large accepted effect that still lacks independent validation; H12 can be considered next if resources allow. Pending interaction claims worth running before broad screening: H15/H19 lineage interactions for SMARCA2/WRN, H16/H52 KRAS or lineage interactions for USP7, H53 lineage interaction for NFE2L2, H21 TP53 interaction for NFE2L2. Pending untested mechanistic claims include H30, H32, H34, H37, H38, H40-H44, H56-H58, and H61; these should be allocated after validation of H8 and any useful interaction follow-up.",
